# A reboot loses no job and leaves no half-written PDF: the RP restarts (a
# cold reset power-cycles the Multi-device) while PRFILES prints, so the job
# is still under its temporary name; at boot it is closed and rendered. A PDF
# left unfinished (an empty 00000009.PDT put on the card) is deleted. The
# next job takes the next number, the first job's PDF holding it: two jobs,
# two PDFs, in order, and no job's bytes left (KEEP_RAW off).
@disk-a tools/dev/builds/disks/escp.st
@keep-raw off
text "Atari +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 1500
key f
key 0x1c
wait 100
cardput PRINTER/00000009.PDT
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
newlog "printer: job 00000001 opened" 1500
reset cold
newlog "Cartridge image in RAM verified" 1500
log "pages: job 00000009's PDF cut short by a reboot, deleted \(0\)" 1500
log "pages: job 00000001 cut short by a reboot, closed \(0\)" 1500
log "pages: job 00000001 rendered, [1-3] pages, PDF [0-9]+ bytes" 1500
cardnone PRINTER/*.PDT
cardnone PRINTER/*.TMP
cardnone PRINTER/*.PRN
text "Atari +: (ST|STE|Mega STE), TOS" 500
key f
key 0x1c
wait 100
key 0x01
wait 900
key 0x39
log "pages: job 00000002 rendered, 3 pages, PDF 32375 bytes" 3000
cardsame PRINTER/00000002.pdf tools/dev/builds/disks/escp-expected.pdf
cardnone PRINTER/*.PRN
